======================================================================
  0. Abstention and truncation — per-agent behaviour
======================================================================
  ABSTAIN is model behaviour: declining to answer is not a dissent, so
  it is excluded from clustering rather than scored as disagreement.
  TRUNC is our measurement failing: the answer hit the token ceiling.
  Both are excluded from panels; they are counted apart because only
  one of them is a property of the model.
  TOKENS is the median completion-token cost per answered question —
  the reasoning-on vs reasoning-off ratio is itself a result.

